{"query":"What's been measuring Axial's inflation before the next eruption?","answer":"Axial Seamount's inflation before the next eruption has been measured by bottom pressure recorders (BPRs) and campaign-style ROV-based pressure measurements using a mobile pressure recorder (MPR). These measurements are integrated with data from the OOI Cabled Array.\n\nInstruments and Measurements\n- Bottom Pressure Recorders (BPRs)\n    - Identity: Continuously recording instruments.\n    - Location: Measured at the center of Axial Caldera.\n    - Capabilities: Provide pressure data, which is used to track inflation and deflation.\n    - Data Availability: Data from these BPRs are updated daily and are available in real-time through the OOI Cabled Array.\n- ROV-based Mobile Pressure Recorder (MPR)\n    - Identity: Campaign-style pressure measurements conducted using a Mobile Pressure Recorder (MPR) deployed by a Remotely Operated Vehicle (ROV).\n    - Capabilities: These measurements are used to remove drift from the BPR pressure data and to tie the BPR dataset together, ensuring accuracy in the long-term time-series of inflation/deflation.\n\nThe evidence does not establish whether COSZO specifically operates or directly uses these instruments, but it clearly links the BPR and MPR data to the OOI Cabled Array for eruption forecasting.","answer_model":"gemini-2.5-flash","answer_citations":[{"id":"PAGE-9901dc2fdc21d8c7","title":"Eruption forecasts at Axial Seamount","url":"https://axial.ceoas.oregonstate.edu/axial_blog.html"}],"answer_links":[],"hits":[{"chunk_id":"PAGE-9901dc2fdc21d8c7-CHUNK-039","collection_id":"axial_monitoring","collection_label":"axial_monitoring","title":"Eruption forecasts at Axial Seamount","score":0.016013824884792627,"citations":[{"source_id":"PAGE-9901dc2fdc21d8c7","title":"Eruption forecasts at Axial Seamount","url":"https://axial.ceoas.oregonstate.edu/axial_blog.html"}],"metadata":{"node_local_id":"PAGE-9901dc2fdc21d8c7-CHUNK-039","locator":null}},{"